        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "05bf250a-4c0e-557d-9b78-8e1561ca19af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Avakian, Bobby Managoff, Robert Manoogian Jr., Louis Armstrong, Miles Davis\n- Companies: Columbia Records\n- Organizations: National Wrestling Alliance\n- Roles: record producer, executive, professional wrestler\n- Topics: jazz, Armenian descent\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Manoogian Jr. was born on January 4, 1918, and later became the American professional wrestler Bobby Managoff.\n- George Avakian was born on March 15, 1919, and became an American record producer and executive.\n- Bobby Managoff was an American professional wrestler of Armenian descent who was best known for his work with the National Wrestling Alliance in the 1940s.\n- George Avakian was particularly known for his work with Columbia Records.\n- George Avakian produced albums by notable jazz musicians including Louis Armstrong and Miles Davis.\n- Robert Manoogian Jr. died on April 3, 2002.",
